 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "<p>“We are returning from war! The Crisis and tens of thousands of black men were drafted into a great struggle. For bleeding France and what she means and has meant and will mean to us and humanity and against the threat of German race arrogance, we fought gladly and to the last drop of blood; for America and her highest ideals, we fought in far-off hope; for the dominant southern oligarchy entrenched in Washington, we fought in bitter resignation. For the America that represents and gloats in lynching, disfranchisement, caste, brutality and devilish insult—for this, in the hateful upturning and mixing of things, we were forced by vindictive fate to fight also.”</p>\n<p align=\"right\">W. E. B. Du Bois, “Returning Soldiers,” The Crisis, XVIII, May, 1919</p>\n<p><i>Refer to the excerpt provided.</i></p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 616100,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which of the following best describes the events that led W. E. B. Du Bois to write the text excerpted here?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1172368,
     "content_html": "Runaway slaves fought bravely in the Civil War and earned their freedom."
    },
    {
     "id": 1172367,
     "content_html": "African Americans who fought in the Spanish-American War deserved civil rights."
    },
    {
     "id": 1172369,
     "content_html": "African Americans fought alongside white soldiers in World War I to protect democratic ideals but returned to a “Jim Crow” society."
    },
    {
     "id": 1172366,
     "content_html": "All who fought in World War II deserve equal treatment under the law."
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 616101,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The ideals of which of the following would most strongly agree with the viewpoints expressed by Du Bois in the provided excerpt?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1172373,
     "content_html": "William Lloyd Garrison"
    },
    {
     "id": 1172372,
     "content_html": "John C. Calhoun"
    },
    {
     "id": 1172371,
     "content_html": "Horace Mann"
    },
    {
     "id": 1172370,
     "content_html": "Henry Clay"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
